  "approach": "Teach the adjectives that have only one singular form (ending in -e or most consonants), how they form plurals, and the exceptions that do add -a (nationalities and -or adjectives).",
  "coverage": [
    "Adjectives in -e have one singular form: inteligente, grande, interesante",
    "Most adjectives ending in a consonant have one singular form: fácil, difícil, joven, azul, gris, feliz",
    "Plural: -e adds -s (inteligentes); a consonant adds -es (fáciles, azules, jóvenes)",
    "z becomes c: feliz → felices",
    "Exceptions with a feminine form: nationalities (español, española) and -or adjectives (trabajador, trabajadora)"
  ],
